d it back from what  it could have been  now this is obviously just my impression  from reading the manga  and who knows i might react differently  to how it was portrayed in the anime  but as of right now i was ecstatic to  finally be leaving the facility and  braving the outside world as the crew  law  g5 smoker and tashigi all escape with  their lives from the place  and again the fights that took place in  this compound were fantastic i loved  luffy's altercation  i really liked what smoker and law were  doing together and when law eventually  cut down virgo that was really  impressive  once again highlighting that this new  generation's time has finally come  that they are ready to compete with the  big boys but now we're coming to what i  think was probably the most shocking  part of the entire story  you see there's a section of this that  leans heavily on the devil fruit  abilities of trafalgar law you see he  has this ability as it's already been  established to remove a part of someone  from their bodies while also keeping  them alive and using this ability many  people in this story have their hearts  removed  from their bodies like smoker and law's  very own and in an effort to prove his  allegiance to caesar he gives his own  heart to him  in exchange for monets now one character  i didn't really speak about during this  video was that of a character happy lady  called monet she appears very early on  and she's effectively a subordinate of  caesar and virgo during this particular  section it was explained to us that in  order to gain caesar's trust  law offered up his own heart in exchange  for monets  taking out both of them and offering up  his own to caesar  as collateral in essence putting his  life in caesar's hands  this whole thing was basically to act as  a truce of sorts during the story now  this was established before the final  act like this was known going into the  final battle but this  was genius as when caesar was lying  outside the compound  after being punched into oblivion and  betrayed by law he still had the heart  given to him by law  and while this is happening monet is  about to blow up the lab in the same  devastating fashion  caesar did four years ago per his  instructions orders her to do this and  as she moves to flip the switch  caesar in a moment of anger stabs the  heart of smoker  but nothing happens as it turns out  the heart he has given to caesar wasn't  smoker at all  but monet's and thus caesar's undoing  was his own  i freaking loved this little swerve and  never saw it coming at all  and something i also like in this part  is caesar's motivation to not  kill law right away once he figures out  that he's after turning on him because  he already has a built-in desire  to kill him by using this new gas that  he's developed to show to the criminal  underground of the world  and to be perfectly honest that as well  as the conclusion of this arc really  helped it finish strong  now that law has in his possession  caesar wearing some sea prism shackles  that usopp managed to swipe  very intelligently you gotta remember  caesar's the only guy who can produce  this sad chemical compound stuff that  goes on the black market and is sold to  emperors of the sea like kaido  who uses it to make animalistic  zone-type devil fruit users for his army  now that he has caesar in his custody  daflamingo a main  vendor on the black market that supplies  kaido with all of this stuff  now has his supply cut off and is now at  the mercy of law which he doesn't  appreciate at all  but he has no choice but to do as he  says  [Music]  while i didn't adore this arc like i  normally do with the vast majority of  one piece's stories  i still think that this one was overall  enjoyable despite  its minor misgivings i have with it some  small pacing issues with some wordy  sections ultimately held this one back  from being a standard great arc  which is a shame but as i said there was  a lot to appreciate and enjoy in this  one thanks to this arc i can now say  that i know law's character enough to  actually speak about him for a little  bit  and i love love love his new design but  perhaps my favorite aspect of this  entire story  is that i could feel like it was  building up to something big doflamengo  is a really different and interesting  character to explore  and i genuinely can't wait to jump into  dressrosa next week  however fair warning dress rosa as a  single arc is over 100 chapters long  that is too much for me to cover in a  single video and so i will be splitting  it up into two separate ones  i hope that's all right with you and  with that said comes the end of the  video  i've been totally not mark i'll see you  all next week for dressrosa part 1 and  thank you so much for watching
 

